From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denfry <aseraw115@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:31:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Count what plugins in compatibility mode do that Folia does
 not allow

A plugin in compatibility mode that fails a thread check only leaves an
error in the log, and the handled cases (synchronous teleport, entity
lists cut down to the region) leave nothing, so it is hard to say what
exactly does not work for the plugin. Failed thread checks, synchronous
teleports and entity lists of plugins in compatibility mode are now
counted by plugin, API method and thread (global, region, other), with
the stack of the first call.

/tessera compat (permission tessera.command.compat) shows the summary,
/tessera compat <plugin> the first stacks, dump writes the report to
debug/, reset clears it. Entries are only added on paths that throw or
already walk the stack, so calls that pass cost nothing.

